      "structure_description": "The S-shaped polyanion consists of two opposed B-α-{AsW9O33} units joined by a cage-like fragment containing four Ho(III) ions and four tartrate segments. The Ho ions lie in a parallelogram plane; K+ ions link the similar polyanions into a three-dimensional framework.",
      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "ph": "About 5.5",
        "procedure": "Add the polytungstoarsenate precursor under stirring to aqueous tartaric acid and HoCl3·6H2O. After 10 min adjust the pH with LiOH, then heat at 60 °C for 1 h.",
